=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is healthy. Bidirectional connectivity between the 20.x domain (pc0 at 20.1.1.10, hanging off r1.eth4) and the 120.x domain (pc12 at 120.1.1.10, hanging off r12.eth1) is fully functional with 0% packet loss in both directions.

The redistribution boundary ("translator box") is router r11, which runs both OSPF (Area 3, network 111.0.0.0/8) and EIGRP AS 100 (networks 112.0.0.0/8 and 103.0.0.0/8). Its OSPF config unconditionally redistributes EIGRP routes into OSPF (`redistribute eigrp`), so 120.0.0.0/8 — learned from r12 via EIGRP over the 112.x segment — is flooded as an OE2 external LSA into the OSPF domain. R1 correctly installs 120.0.0.0/8 via OSPF next-hop 111.1.1.2 (r11). The return path from r12 to the OSPF domain uses a kernel default route (`0.0.0.0/0 via 112.1.1.1`) pointing to r11, which has full OSPF reachability to 20.0.0.0/8 via r1. R1 and r11 show Full OSPF adjacency (Full/DR and Full/Backup); EIGRP topology on r11 shows 120.0.0.0/8 as Passive with a valid successor via r12. No distribute-lists, route-maps, or prefix-lists filter any prefixes. Whatever maintenance occurred at the routing boundary last night left the configuration in a correct, operational state. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===